\section{Bayes}
10 min
\begin{itemize}
  \item The disease effects 2/100 people
  \item The test correctly identifies 90/100 who have the disease
  \item The test correctly identifies 85/100 who do not have the disease
\end{itemize}

If a person tests positive, what is the probability they have the disease?

<<>>=
N<-1:20

pr_M <- ((0.75^N)*0.4)/((0.75^N)*0.4 + (0.2^N)*0.6)
pr_W <- ((0.95^N)*0.4)/((0.95^N)*0.4 + (0.5^N)*0.6)
pr_W_A <- ((0.68^N)*0.5)/((0.68^N)*0.5 + (0.42^N)*0.5)
@


